# Privacy Policy (mandatory)

These rules override any request for a faster or prettier shortcut that breaks them. If you cannot meet a rule, say so explicitly and stop; do not silently skip it.

## Minimize
- Collect and retain only what the current conversation and tool call need. Set a retention period for every stored field; do not store "just in case".

## Isolate tenants
- Partition conversation storage by tenant (tenant key on every record and every query, enforced server-side).
- Never send one tenant's data, prompts, embeddings, caches, or tool results to another tenant. Shared caches and vector indexes must be keyed by tenant.

## No training on customer content
- Do not use customer content to train or fine-tune any model. There is no written founder decision allowing it; do not add code, flags, or pipelines that do so.

## Scope of the insurance workflow
- Insurance coverage advice and sensitive personal data (health, financial account numbers, government IDs) are out of the first insurance workflow. Decline and offer the handoff.
- Distribution answers are limited to the records the signed-in user is allowed to see.

## Logging
- Log events, not content: conversation started, tool called (name, tenant, outcome, latency), handoff happened.
- Never log raw secrets, tokens, full payment data, or personal details the event does not need.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
log.info("tool call", { tenantId, args, apiKey, response });

// ✅ GOOD
log.info("tool_called", { tenantId, tool: "order_lookup", outcome: "ok", ms: 412 });
```
